# Pointer ++, +=, -- and &arr[i] scale by the pointee size (1, 2, 4); with
# constant steps the pointer folds into the absolute address (ported from
# opensnes-emu test_ptr_arithmetic, which only required it to compile).
# u8 *: +1, +3, -1 -> bytes+1, +4, +3.
in test_char_ptr: present lda #2\n\tsta\.w bytes\+1\n\tlda #5\n\tsta\.w bytes\+4\n\tlda #4\n\tsta\.w bytes\+3\n
# u16 *: ++ is +2 bytes, += 2 is +4 bytes.
in test_short_ptr: present lda\.w #22136\n\tsta\.w words\+2\n\tlda\.w #43981\n\tsta\.w words\+6\n
# Sprite * (4 bytes): p++ lands on sprites+4, its tile field on +6.
in test_struct_ptr: present lda #30\n\tsta\.w sprites\+4\n\tlda #40\n\tsta\.w sprites\+5\n\trep #\$20\n\tlda\.w #257\n\tsta\.w sprites\+6\n
in test_struct_ptr: present lda #50\n\tsta\.w sprites\+8\n
in test_array_indexing: present lda #100\n\tsta\.w bytes\+5\n\trep #\$20\n\tlda\.w #200\n\tsta\.w words\+6\n\tsep #\$20\n\tlda #55\n\tsta\.w sprites\+4\n
